    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d944">

                <pb facs="1173" n="1163" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg1163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/7–147</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Director of the Office of Financial and Development
                        Policy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ness</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Chairman of the Chinese Supply Commission</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wang</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-07-16">July 16, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Dr. Wang</hi>: This is to acknowledge with
                    thanks your letter of July 1, 1947, enclosing a check of the Chinese Supply
                    Commission of $2,820,020.32 in payment of the principal and interest due on July
                    1, 1947 under the “Agreement between the Governments of the United States and
                    the Republic of China on the Disposition of Lend-Lease Supplies in Inventory or
                    Procurement in the United States”, dated June 14, 1946, and known as the
                    “Pipeline” Agreement.</p>
                <p>The check has been transmitted to the Treasury Department with instructions to
                    deposit it in a special account so that, in the event that the lend-lease
                    settlement negotiations should result in any modification of the Pipeline
                    Agreement, any agreed portion of this payment could be refunded to the
                    Government of China. This is to conform with the suggestion contained in the
                    second paragraph of your letter.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Norman</hi> T. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Ness</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
